dge."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "Opus 5.5 finally played B7, the engine's first choice many times over, and lost only 0.4 points. It held the left side and left the 10k's B8 on the next move to lose 7.7."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "Opus 5.5's B6 lost 11.2 points, the worst move of the game, and took the lead from -13.7 to -2.4. The 10k's C8 gave back 1.5, the lead settled at -4.0, and it stayed there to the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties for the current position; the other commands were cat/tail of notes and appending to CLAUDE.md and games.md. None of them generates, scores or ranks candidate moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}